## 4. Checkpoint / resume

If a session dies mid-wave: partial state lives in (a) the wave branch's checkpoint
commits and (b) a `[PARTIAL]` logbook entry with: internal tasks closed, exact step in
progress, which executor tier held each open task and on which rung of the ladder
(attempt log), unmerged worktrees, and the next command to run. The resuming session
reads the `[PARTIAL]` entry, checks out the branch and continues the loop from that
rung — it does NOT restart, and it does NOT re-brief tasks whose worktree is intact.

